Russia could pressure could kind  of compete for America's favor by  pressuring by pressuring the enemy to go  to the negotiating table now there's a  tragedy in that in that it overestimated  it underestimated how organic the the  forces in in Vietnam were how they  didn't need China and Russia to tell  them what to do so it's just one more of  these tragedies of our Cold War hubris  but by the same token it was it was it  was a very far seeing thing although it  wasn't so far seeing because in the  Shanghai communication the Shan  communicate which came out of Nixon's  February 1972 trip to China there's only  one sentence on trade because Henry  Kissinger told Nixon the amount of trade  I can imagine  America ever having with China is  infinitesimal  on that I know that we should be  concluding our sessions today thank you  so much for coming and yes in Rick will  be signing books outside so if you have  any further questions true enter them  there thanks for coming  [Applause]
 

